      "text": "To find the 25th term of the arithmetic sequence \\(2, 5, 8, \\ldots\\), we need to determine the common difference and use the formula for the \\(n\\)-th term of an arithmetic sequence. \n\n1. **Identify the common difference:**\n   The common difference \\(d\\) is the difference between any two consecutive terms. For the sequence \\(2, 5, 8, \\ldots\\):\n   \\[\n   d = 5 - 2 = 3\n   \\]\n\n2. **Use the formula for the \\(n\\)-th term of an arithmetic sequence:**\n   The formula for the \\(n\\)-th term \\(a_n\\) of an arithmetic sequence is:\n   \\[\n   a_n = a_1 + (n-1)d\n   \\]\n   where \\(a_1\\) is the first term, \\(d\\) is the common difference, and \\(n\\) is the term number.\n\n3. **Substitute the known values into the formula:**\n   For \\(n = 25\\), \\(a_1 = 2\\), and \\(d = 3\\):\n   \\[\n   a_{25} = 2 + (25-1) \\cdot 3\n   \\]\n\n4. **Calculate the term number \\(n-1\\):**\n   \\[\n   25 - 1 = 24\n   \\]\n\n5. **Multiply by the common difference \\(d\\):**\n   \\[\n   24 \\cdot 3 = 72\n   \\]\n\n6. **Add this result to the first term \\(a_1\\):**\n   \\[\n   a_{25} = 2 + 72 = 74\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the value of the 25th term of the arithmetic sequence is \\(\\boxed{74}\\).",
